# Ruby string quotes

Prefer single-quoted strings. Use double quotes only when the string needs interpolation, escape sequences (`\n`, `\t`, `\"`), or other double-quote-only syntax.

```ruby
# ❌ BAD
name = "Yan"
path = "app/models/loan_offer.rb"
redirect_to "/admin/loan_offers"

# ✅ GOOD
name = 'Yan'
path = 'app/models/loan_offer.rb'
redirect_to '/admin/loan_offers'

# ✅ GOOD — interpolation or escapes need double quotes
greeting = "Hello, #{name}"
message = "Line one\nLine two"
```
